# plurnk-bench config — the shipped legend: every knob + its default.
#
# plurnk-bench is a CLIENT of the plurnk daemon: it drives benchmark tasks through
# @plurnk/plurnk, which connects to a running plurnk-service daemon. Alias definitions,
# provider configuration, and credentials remain in the product's XDG/shell cascade.
# The committed bench floor selects its candidate through the ordinary PLURNK_MODEL.
#
# Override order (low → high precedence):
#   ./.env.example  (this floor — override, don't remove!)
#   < ./.env        (per-checkout config)
#   < --env-file=…
#   < shell environment
# Feature-flag bools use `=== "1"` exactly, never `=== "true"`.

# --- Daemon connection (consumed by @plurnk/plurnk) ---
# Service 1.0.0: single listener — the client surface is PLURNK_HOST/PLURNK_PORT (shipped
# default 127.0.0.1:1066, the AG-UI surface); the separate PLURNK_WS listener is gone.
# Bench sets NOTHING: the in-container daemon+client pair share the shipped default.

# --- Candidate model uses the product cascade ---
# Shell PLURNK_MODEL wins, then the XDG operator file, then the committed benchmark
# default. The XDG file still owns alias definitions and tuning; the shell owns provider
# endpoints and credentials. smoke.sh forwards the resolved minimal model layer to the
# in-container daemon. Every daemon knob remains documented by plurnk-service.

# --- Bench's own knobs (PLURNK_BENCH_ namespace; smoke.sh orchestration, never forwarded) ---
# All bench-invented config is namespaced PLURNK_BENCH_ to respect the global env and to
# stay distinct from the daemon's PLURNK_* config that we merely carry.
# PLURNK_BENCH_TIMEOUT_SEC=   # client timeout override; default = task's [agent] budget − headroom
# PLURNK_BENCH_CPUS=          # container cpu override; default = task native (leaderboard-compliant)
# PLURNK_BENCH_FORCE_BUILD=   # =1 force rebuild for non-versioned image inputs; publications auto-invalidate
# PLURNK_BENCH_NO_GBNF=       # =1 drop PLURNK_PROVIDERS_GBNF (models that can't enforce it, e.g. xai/grok)
